2026-11-01T13:03Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context
Author request, 2026-11-01. Besides the HAL publications indexed by the RAG,
Cirdi should let users search the CIRED library's catalogue of physical
copies (books, reports, grey literature on paper), so an answer can point to
"available on paper at CIRED, shelf X" when no digital full text exists.

To find out, not assumed: where that catalogue lives (library software and
OPAC, a shared spreadsheet, a union catalogue such as SUDOC), who maintains
it, whether it has an API or an export, and how often it changes.

## Approach to decide
Metadata only (no full text): either query the catalogue live at answer time,
or import a periodic export into a separate search index or collection
(fits ticket 0009's architecture choice), and show catalogue hits in their
own results block, distinct from cited HAL passages. With ticket 0013 (internal
service) the catalogue can stay inside the lab network.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Catalogue source, owner, access method and update rhythm identified and recorded here
- [ ] Search over title, authors, year and keywords returns catalogue records with their location/shelf mark, shown apart from HAL citations
- [ ] Refresh path documented (live query or scheduled import) and tested once
- [ ] A test query for a known paper-only item finds it
